  "interpretation": "The still-water state is a fixed point of the residual only to round-off, so a single step injects O(eps*(2p+1)*|F|/dx) of spurious momentum.  Those residuals are coherent, so the spurious current accumulates *algebraically*: the fitted log-log slopes are bounded (0.98..3.83 over T = 0.5..4.0 s), no exponential growth.  The accumulated level is max |u|/sqrt(gh) = 5.0e-08 over every case and time (p=2, T=4.0 s).  A bare 'machine precision for all time' claim is therefore not reproducible: the achievable spurious current must be quoted with its integration time, mesh and dtype.  The seed is round-off, not bed-representation error -- the flat-bed case (z_b = 0, exactly representable) drifts too.  Values vary by a factor of a few between BLAS/thread configurations; the tolerances in tests/test_swe_wellbalanced_hydrostatic.py keep >= 180x headroom over the measurements quoted here.  Only an algebraic window is established (T <= 4.0 s); see docs/swe-hydrostatic-roundoff-drift-law.md."
 }
}
